    "notes": "The example design used by the NIC 2026 sessions, as the private automation declares it. IP addresses, DNS servers and GUIDs in this file are sanitized example values, not the deployment inputs: 192.168.100.0/24 stands in for the management subnet (gateway .1, nodes .11/.12, infrastructure pool .20-.29; management is untagged on the hosts), 10.100.4.36/.37 for the two DNS servers in Azure reached over the site-to-site VPN, and 172.30.71.0/24 and 172.30.72.0/24 for the storage subnets on Port4 (VLAN 711) and Port6 (VLAN 712). Storage VLANs, adapter names, intents, QoS and hardware match the deployment. Logical networks (SDN enabled by Arc, prefix nic26): the six names and VLAN IDs match the deployment (compute 110, AVD 120, SOFS 130, app 131, data 132, isolated 133); their 10.100.x.0/24 subnets, gateways and pools are sanitized example values (owner, 14 Oct 2026: the design matches the as-built cluster)."
